Enrolment Process
1. Obtain a subscription from any Coin partner
2. They will return a Device Authorisation JwToken good for 48 hrs
3. Download Fido Provider
https://github.com/Money-2021/PaymentClient/blob/main/Fido.dll
4.  Use the Authorisation token and Fido Provider to create the local Fido device as follows:
  // Initialise device
  Fido.FidoProvider d = new Fido.FidoProvider(authToken, true);
  d.Enrol(); // Enrol with Infrastructure
  string spath = @"D:\Examples\Devices\DeviceStore-" + d.GetDeviceSin() + ".json";
  d.SaveStore(spath);

Recovery Process
1. On each device enrolment a protected recovery pin is provided and stored with the Fido Device Store.
2. It is the user's responsibility to retrieve the unprotected pin from the fido store and securely store it outside of the device.
Upon loss or compromise this pin is required to move or create a new fido device.
If this pin is lost the user must contact their node operator and provide account identification to recover this pin, this is on a fee for service basis.

Note
1. The Auth Token is ITSDSA signed hence cannot be created outside of the infrastructure, and is validated within the Enrolment request.
